course: dictionary
lesson: 1323
title: What is a calendar?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A calendar is a chart that shows the days, weeks and months of the year. You use one to count forward to a birthday, a holiday or a test day. Ask yourself: what is this word doing in the sentence?
explain: A calendar can also divide time in different ways. «Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah and Lunar New Year fall on different dates each year because they follow lunar or lunisolar calendars (calendars that follow the Moon, or the Moon and the Sun together).» So the context shows that a calendar is a way of splitting time into days, months and years, and that different cultures do it differently.
explain: A calendar can also be a list of planned events, such as a school calendar. «Letters, video calls and a calendar help when a parent works far away or is deployed (sent away to work) in the military.» Here a calendar helps a family plan when they will next talk or meet. Clues like days, dates, plans and months tell you which meaning fits.
fact: A calendar is a chart of the days, weeks and months of the year.
fact: A calendar also means a way of dividing time into days, months and years.
fact: Some calendars follow the Moon, and others follow the Sun, or both together.
fact: «Caesar's Julian calendar, from 45 BC, had 365 days and a leap day every 4 years, so its average year was 365 days and 6 hours.»
fact: A school calendar is a list of planned events, such as term dates and trips.
exercise: «Caesar's Julian calendar, from 45 BC, had 365 days and a leap day every 4 years.» How many days did a normal year have in this calendar? | *365 | 400 | 360 | 366
exercise: What might a school calendar show? | Only the shape of the Moon | *Planned events, such as trips and sports days | Recipes for birthday cakes | The weather for next week
exercise: «The Islamic calendar follows the moon and is about eleven days shorter than the sun's year.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the calendar follows. | eleven | *moon | sun | Islamic
test: «Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah and Lunar New Year fall on different dates each year.» Why do these festivals move from year to year? | *Because they follow lunar or lunisolar calendars | Because the schools close each year | Because the shops change their prices | Because the Sun gets bigger
test: An advent calendar helps you count down the days to a special day. What is its main job? | To tell the time on a clock | *To count down the days to a special day | To show the weather | To list foods to buy
exam: «The Islamic calendar follows the moon and is about eleven days shorter than the sun's year, so Ramadan moves earlier each year.» What does this tell us? | Ramadan always falls in the same week | The sun's year is shorter than the Islamic calendar | Ramadan has no fixed dates at all | *Ramadan can fall in any season over the years
